; Exercise 18 — Fibonacci
; Return the nth Fibonacci number, where n is a non-negative integer.
; The sequence starts 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, ...
; Example: (fibonacci 6) -> 8
; Your rules go here:

!(assertEqual (fibonacci 0) 0)
!(assertEqual (fibonacci 1) 1)
!(assertEqual (fibonacci 6) 8)
!(assertEqual (fibonacci 10) 55)
